  "questions": [],
  "alt": "A tree diagram. Repeated judgment, at the top, splits into two routes. The left route:\n    when a property is already decidable over the current artifact, Alignment encodes the predicate directly\n    into a test, validator, constraint, or gate. The right route: when the property requires reconstruction,\n    Modeling changes the representation first, producing a structured relation. Both routes converge on a\n    shared step, a predicate evaluated over a model — Alignment's test is a predicate over the artifact taken\n    as its own trivial model, Modeling's check is a predicate over the externalized structured relation — and\n    both land on the same outcome, a repeatable decision. A caption beneath names the boundary between the\n    two sides the determinization frontier.",
